## Why This Is Asked

Tests reasoning with Kleene 3-valued logic in a constraint set that mirrors feature-flag policies. Requires a lightweight backtracking propagator that respects Unknowns and prevents false violations.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene 3-valued semantics
- Implication under uncertainty
- Lightweight backtracking propagator design
- Constraint satisfaction with Unknowns

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal 3-valued values and a propagation stub
const V = {T:1, F:0, U:2}
function not(x){ return x===V.T?V.F : x===V.F?V.T : V.U }
function or(a,b){ return a===V.T||b===V.T?V.T : (a===V.U||b===V.U?V.U : V.F) }
function and(a,b){ return a===V.F||b===V.F?V.F : (a===V.T && b===V.T ? V.T : V.U) }
function implies(p,q){ const np = not(p); return or(np,q) }
```

